  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Configuration-bindable settings for the Responses API server, loaded from an
            <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.IConfigurationSection" /> via
            <see cref="M:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.ResponsesServerHostExtensions.AddResponsesServer(Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.IHostApplicationBuilder,System.String)" />.
            <para>
            The inherited <see cref="P:System.ClientModel.Primitives.ClientSettings.Credential" /> / <see cref="P:System.ClientModel.Primitives.ClientSettings.CredentialProvider" />
            bind the identity used for BOTH Foundry response storage and resilient-task storage from the same
            section, so the two can never diverge. <see cref="P:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.ResponsesServerSettings.Endpoint" /> overrides the platform's
            <c>FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT</c> environment variable, and the option flags below replace the
            <see cref="T:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.ResponsesServerOptions" /> shape when the host binds from configuration.
            </para></summary>
    <remarks>To be added.</remarks>
  </Docs>
